    "source_text": "Following general procedure F using 2,2,2‐Trifluoro‐N‐(2‐methoxybenzyl)acetamide (58.3 mg, 0.25 mmol), B2pin2 (127 mg, 0.50 mmol), [Ir(COD)OMe]2 (2.5 mg, 0.00375 mmol) and dtbpy (2.0 mg, 0.0075 mmol) in THF (1.25 mL). The reaction was stirred at 50 °C for 20 hours before cooling and the solvents removed. Analysis of crude 1 H NMR using internal standard 1,2‐dimethoxyethane showed 1:2 meta:para borylation in 70% yield. The crude product was purified by silica gel chromatography (Pet. Ether (40‐60):EtOAc (19:1) to give the title compound (as a 1:2 mixture of meta:para ratio, as determined by 1 H NMR) as a colourless oil (53.1 mg, 0.15 mmol, 59%).",
